// pcstore.cpp - Computer parts store (command-line, object-oriented C++17)
//
// Style:  uses ONLY "using namespace std;" - no prefixes on library names, no other using or namespace.
//
// Build:  g++ -std=c++17 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -o pcstore pcstore.cpp
// Run:    ./pcstore          (Windows: pcstore.exe)
//
// Class overview
//   Product (abstract)  <- Cpu, Gpu, Motherboard, Memory, Storage, PowerSupply,
//                          PcCase, Cooler, Monitor, Peripheral
//   Catalog             owns every Product, finds / filters / searches them
//   Basket              holds BasketItems (product + quantity), add / remove / change qty
//   CompatibilityChecker  warns about CPU/board socket, RAM type, case size, PSU wattage
//   Console             safe keyboard input helpers
//   Store               menus and the whole customer flow (browse, basket, checkout)
//
// To change the stock, edit Catalog::populate() near the bottom of the classes.
// Prices are approximate US-dollar retail prices and WILL differ from real shops:
// update them to your own prices before you use the program for real.

